{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Overnight autonomous bug sweep — segment ending 2026-09-20 ~10:45 UTC\n\n### Sweep watermark\n\nPrevious authoritative watermark: `2026-09-02T10:00:00-07:00`.\n**New watermark: `2026-09-20T10:45:00Z`.** AWS alarms and GitHub Actions were\nboth swept at that time; findings below.\n\n### AWS alarm sweep\n\nOne alarm in `ALARM`, none in `INSUFFICIENT_DATA`:\n\n- `rebar-docker-buildkit-cache-high` — 6/6 datapoints at 86.0 against an 85.0\n  threshold, latched since `2026-09-09T22:44:21-07:00`. Already tracked by the\n  open bug `catty-giddied-hedgehog` (\"BuildKit cache exceeds its cap and never\n  reclaims; the alarm has been latched\"). No new ticket filed.\n\n### GitHub Actions sweep\n\nAcross the last 120 runs exactly 3 workflows have failures, and every one has a\nfix that landed or is in review this session:\n\n- `Mirror Guard` (3 failures, latest `35501880425`) → bug `974f-a1c8-da40-43a0`,\n  Gerrit change 3007.\n- `Terraform Drift` (1 failure, latest `35494675507`) → bug `859c-760d-04dd-44a6`,\n  Gerrit change 3006.\n- `Verify Authorship Identity` (2 failures, latest `35495552110`) → bug\n  `bc25-1351-dd0e-4909`, Gerrit change 3001, **merged** as `cc4a23a2405`.\n\nNo previously unknown workflow failures.\n\n### Landed this segment\n\nGerrit changes submitted and merged, in order: **3003** (`d082`, merged\n`740983fe830`), **3002** (`da2f`, merged `d08a0a373a3`), **3004** (`0fb0`, merged\n`c0b1ad2e8e9`), **3001** (`bc25`, merged `cc4a23a2405`). That brings the session\ntotal to 17 merges.\n\nTickets closed with signed completion attestations: `d082-5fe8-0f98-49fc`,\n`0fb0-5c46-66ae-405d`, `da2f-b473-0494-4e36`.\n\n### In review\n\n- **3005** — `c6fb-49cf-61e3-4b29`, gate-sidecar visibility.\n- **3006** — `859c-760d-04dd-44a6`, Bedrock Terraform variable defaults.\n- **3007** — `974f-a1c8-da40-43a0`, mirror-guard merged-reachability lag tolerance.\n\nAll three were proven by ONE combined `make verify` on a stacked worktree\n(`verify-stack2`, the 3 commits cherry-picked onto `origin/main`), which returned\n`17 failed, 20262 passed, 126 skipped in 1701.85s` — exactly the settled pandoc\nbaseline and zero real failures. Stacking disjoint modules into one verify rather\nthan running three serially saved roughly 50 minutes.\n\n### Two operational findings\n\n**1. The close gate's `ref` must be a FULL SHA of a commit the MCP workspace has\nalready fetched.** The MCP server verifies against its own checkout at\n`/var/gerrit/site/mcp-code`, which trails `origin/main`. Passing `ref=\"origin/main\"`\nmade completion verification read a PRE-MERGE tree and report 20 false unmet\ncriteria for `d082`. Passing the abbreviated `c0b1ad2e8e9` failed outright with\n\"cannot resolve ref ... Name a valid branch, tag, or full SHA reachable from\n'origin'\". Passing the full 40-character SHA succeeded. Use the full merged SHA.\n\n**2. The Gerrit \"Missing tree\" object-store fault recurred** (see\n`deserved-rubidium-pussycat`, closed). Three pushes from three unrelated worktrees\non two different bases were all rejected with `Missing tree 9f4ab41bab6e...`. The\ntree resolved locally, the clone is not partial, and the tree was reachable from a\ncommit Gerrit had already merged. It cleared after `git fetch gerrit` plus a retry,\nwith no EBS snapshot, mirror-fetch, or ownership normalization. Because the fetch\nand the retry happened in one step, \"fetch fixed negotiation\" and \"transient window\nclosed on its own\" cannot be separated; full evidence is on that ticket and no root\ncause was claimed.\n\n### Blocked\n\n`6d98-28f4-946a-4016` — its Langfuse criterion is PROVEN (the `langfuse tracing\nround-trip (ephemeral self-hosted)` job succeeded on run `35502010162` against the\nfix commit `0bce6a72425`, so the `pull access denied for minio/minio` failure is\ngone). Its third criterion is conditional on the Jira DC harness, and that job has\nbeen in progress for over 2 hours on the same run. Waiting rather than guessing."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789900126466039918,"uuid":"50565357-f77c-4c67-82da-db54ed6cf71c"}